fix: review round 9 -- universal KVP_MODEL_CONFIG, .local overlay in verify gate, retention bug, emergency-evict --yes guard, persist_enabled refusal, advanced identity fields

Operator request + review:
- Universal model-config selector (KVP_MODEL_CONFIG): config.py, env.sh,
  setup-identity.sh and verify-engine-identity.sh no longer hardcode
  mimo-v2.6-pro. Resolution: explicit KVP_MODEL_CONFIG env > sole non-generic
  candidate with identity.env; ambiguous multi-model layouts now refuse
  explicitly (no silent default).
- Review P1 (verify-engine-identity reads wrong config): the gate now merges
  identity.env + identity.env.local into a temp file (same overlay semantics
  setup-identity.sh writes to), so it verifies the SAME effective values, not
  the stale tracked file. Smoke-tested: .local value wins over base.
- Review P2 (retention.py sharing formula bug): 1/sqrt(shared_refs) penalised
  shared entries while the comment claimed the opposite; corrected to
  sqrt(shared_refs) so shared entries score HIGHER (freeing one ref frees 0
  real bytes), and value_score now records effective_freed_bytes (0 if shared).
- Review P2 (emergency-evict deletes whole dirs without warning): now requires
  --yes with an explicit destructive-action warning and points to targeted
  purge instead; exit 2 when --yes is missing.
- Review (start-cache KVP_PERSIST_ENABLED misleading half-state): false now
  REFUSES startup (data-on-shutdown-deletion contradicts the persistence
  requirement and the L2 template is persist_enabled=true) instead of
  warn-then-ignore.
- Review (start-cache host-mode ignored HTTP/serde flags): host branch now
  passes --http-host/--http-port/--l2-serde exactly like the docker branch.
- Review (identity incomplete): optional advanced identity fields added
  (lora_adapters, multimodal_components, rope_config_digest, speculative_config)
  -- empty == not applicable, not an error; rope_config_digest validated as
  64-hex when set. All 55 tests green.